<title>SPAIN: Issing says Germany must make more efforts for EMU.</title>
<headline>Issing says Germany must make more efforts for EMU.</headline>
<dateline>PAMPLONA, Spain 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank board member Otmar Issing said on Thursday that Germany needed to make greater efforts to be in shape to join Europe's single currency.</p>
<p>&quot;In Germany we also have many problems. Unemployment, the pension system, the tax system...and we still have to make great efforts to be in conditions (to join EMU),&quot; he told journalists after a speech to bankers in the northern Spanish town.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
